# FastAPI greenfield (default mode)

## STEP sequence

| Step | Condition | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | always | Entity design: full relational schema, symmetric relationships; classify every endpoint TESTABLE or SKIPPED. Kafka design note appended if gated — see [Kafka](../../capabilities/kafka.md). |
| 2 | always | Database files — SQLAlchemy 2.x async, or Motor+Pydantic for MongoDB. |
| 3 | always | Models + schemas. |
| 4 | `auth.method` | Auth scaffolding — see [Auth](../../capabilities/auth.md). |
| 5 | always | Routers + main wiring; pagination is always rendered here — see [Pagination](../../capabilities/pagination.md). |
| 5.5 | Kafka gated | Producer/consumer wiring. |
| 6 | always | Seed data. |
| 7 | always | Infra: requirements, env file, start scripts, Dockerfile/compose/makefile per flag. Deferred to 11b instead if Azure DevOps is enabled. |
| 7c / 7d | flag-gated | Unit tests / CI workflow — see [Reports & Deploy](../../capabilities/reports-and-deploy.md). |
| 8 | `testing_framework` | Test generation — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md). Now uses the same resolved value STEP 11 does, so the two can no longer disagree. |
| 9 | always | README. |
| 10 | always | Syntax + import check, fix/retry until clean. |
| 10.5 | linting gated | Linting — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md). |
| 11 | `testing_framework` | Test execution — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md) and [Reports & Deploy](../../capabilities/reports-and-deploy.md) (curl branch enforces ngrok-first ordering). |
| 11b | Azure DevOps gated | Deferred Dockerfile write, once every test in STEP 11 has passed. |
| 12 | always | Baseline test summary (in-context). |
| 13 | always | Summary (baseline). |
| 14 | always | Iterative fix loop, max 5 — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md). This step ends the fix loop; it is not the final step. |
| 15 / 15.5 | always | Reports (xlsx + docx) — see [Reports & Deploy](../../capabilities/reports-and-deploy.md), including the email sub-step if gated. |
| 16 | always | Final summary. **This is the true stop condition** — the STEP 14 fix loop is a gate along the way, not the finish line. |

## Hard safety rules (mode-specific; formatting guard and env isolation are shared, see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md))

- Port 8000 protection: "NEVER pick a different port. NEVER search for another free port. Killing port 8000 will terminate your entire session and destroy all progress."
- No brace expansion — `write_file` creates parent dirs; don't rely on shell brace expansion for directory creation.
- Stop the boot-verify server with `kill $SERVER_PID` only.
- Confined to `{output_dir}`.

## Completion criteria

Stop only when STEP 16's final summary has been printed.

## Capability hooks

| Capability | Where it lands | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| Kafka | STEP 1 tail → STEP 5.5 → STEP 7 → STEP 11 | `kafka_url` |
| Auth | STEP 4 + STEP 5 | `auth.method` |
| Pagination | Always rendered in STEP 5 | `pagination_style`/`pagination_default_limit` |
| Linting | STEP 10.5 | `linting_tool` |
